  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>y</mi></math> and <math><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>v</mi></math> be two complex numbers, such that <math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math><msup><mrow><mi>z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>w</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math> Then, the number of ordered pairs <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to (where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>)",
    "image": null
  },
